::CW_U01_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.CW.WR.08] Passage: "The bus pulled away before Ana raised her hand. She kept waving anyway, long after the taillights blurred." Which evidence best supports the claim that the scene shows missed opportunity?{
~A. The passage includes a character named Ana.#Incorrect. The name alone does not prove missed opportunity.
~B. The passage mentions taillights.#Incorrect. Taillights help the image, but the timing is stronger evidence.
=C. The bus pulled away before Ana raised her hand.#Correct. The timing shows Ana acts too late.
~D. The sentence has two parts.#Incorrect. Sentence structure alone is not the evidence.
}

::CW_U01_L06_GP_Q02::[MLA.CW.WR.08] Passage: "The word sorry sat between them, small and sharp." Which claim is best supported?{
=A. The apology feels painful.#Correct. "small and sharp" makes the word feel capable of hurting.
~B. The characters are at a concert.#Incorrect. No concert detail appears.
~C. The word is written on a poster.#Incorrect. The passage does not mention a poster.
~D. The apology has no emotional weight.#Incorrect. "small and sharp" gives it emotional weight.
}

::CW_U01_L06_GP_Q03::[MLA.CW.COM.02] Passage: "Eli folded the invitation once, then again, until it fit under his watchband." Which workshop feedback is most useful?{
~A. This is good.#Incorrect. This is too general.
~B. Eli is weird.#Incorrect. This judges the character and does not discuss craft.
~C. I would delete all of it.#Incorrect. This is unsupported and not constructive.
=D. The repeated folding action shows secrecy and attachment; you might add one sensory detail to make the invitation more vivid.#Correct. This uses evidence, reasoning, and a revision suggestion.
}

::CW_U01_L06_GP_Q04::[MLA.CW.WR.09] Passage: "The classroom lights stayed on, but every desk was empty except hers." Which evidence best supports the claim that the setting creates isolation?{
~A. lights stayed on#Incorrect. This detail alone does not show isolation.
=B. every desk was empty except hers#Correct. This exact detail shows the character separated from everyone else.
~C. classroom#Incorrect. The setting alone does not prove isolation.
~D. The sentence is short.#Incorrect. Length is not the main evidence.
}

::CW_U01_L06_GP_Q05::[MLA.CW.WR.08] Which response has all three parts of evidence-based craft reasoning?{
~A. The scene is strong.#Incorrect. This has a claim but no evidence or reasoning.
~B. "small and sharp."#Incorrect. This is evidence only.
=C. The writer makes the apology feel painful because the phrase "small and sharp" turns the word into something that can hurt.#Correct. This includes claim, evidence, and reasoning.
~D. The writer creates pain because I think so.#Incorrect. This lacks evidence.
}
